-- title:
--   Nonzerodivisor on all geometric fibres: flatness of B/gB
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $B$ a commutative Noetherian ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure such that $B$ is flat as an $A$-module, and let $g \in B$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $K$ (taken in the same universe as $A$) and every $A$-algebra structure on $K$, the element $g \otimes_A 1$ is a non-zero-divisor in the ring $B \otimes_A K$, i.e. it belongs to the submonoid $\mathrm{nonZeroDivisors}(B \otimes_A K)$ of elements whose multiplication map is injective. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: first, $g$ itself is a non-zero-divisor in $B$; second, the quotient ring $B / (g)$, by the ideal generated by $g$, is flat as an $A$-module. Note that no hypothesis beyond commutativity is imposed on the base ring $A$, and that the fibre hypothesis is stated for arbitrary algebraically closed $A$-fields rather than only for the algebraic closures of the residue fields of $A$.
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic form of the statement that a divisor which is an effective Cartier divisor on each geometric fibre of a flat family is a relative effective Cartier divisor with flat quotient (EGA IV, 11.3.8), obtained from the local flatness criterion by localisation; the Noetherian hypothesis on $B$ enters through Krull's intersection theorem in the local rings of $B$. It is used in the geometric form asserting that the ideal of the zero scheme of a section is invertible and its quotient flat over the base.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Flat_mem_nonZeroDivisors_and_flat_quotient_span_of_forall_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Basic
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open TensorProduct nonZeroDivisors

theorem Module.Flat.mem_nonZeroDivisors_and_flat_quotient_span_of_forall_isAlgClosed
    {A : Type u} {B : Type v} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    [Module.Flat A B] (g : B)
    (hg : ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] [Algebra A K],
      (g ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : K)) ∈ nonZeroDivisors (B ⊗[A] K)) :
    g ∈ nonZeroDivisors B ∧ Module.Flat A (B ⧸ Ideal.span {g}) := by sorry
